## 6. RESTRICTIONS & COMPATIBILITY:
restrictions:
  max_io_current: "0mA"
  total_current_limit: "12000mA"
  warnings[9]:
    - "CPU 1516-3 PN/DP has NO integrated field I/O (no DI, DO, AI, AO on the CPU module itself) — all physical I/O requires ET 200MP I/O modules installed on the same S7-1500 mounting rail or distributed PROFINET/PROFIBUS I/O slaves; a bare CPU with no I/O modules performs no field acquisition"
    - "A SIMATIC Memory Card is MANDATORY — the CPU has no internal program memory; without a valid SIMATIC Memory Card the CPU cannot execute any program and will fault on power-up; the card stores the program, project, and data; use only Siemens original SIMATIC Memory Cards (6ES79... part numbers)"
    - "PROFINET IRT (Isochronous Real-Time) on X1 requires ALL network nodes (switches, I/O devices) to be IRT-capable — standard PROFINET switches such as unmanaged switches will break IRT sync; use only SCALANCE X-200 IRT or X-300 IRT managed switches in the IRT segment; mixing IRT and non-IRT devices on the same segment downgrades all devices to RT mode"
    - "PROFIBUS DP on X3 requires correct bus termination — the first and last physical devices on the PROFIBUS cable segment MUST have bus terminators activated (120Ω resistor network); missing or double termination causes reflection artifacts, CRC errors and slave timeouts; never terminate a device in the middle of the segment"
    - "The system power supply (PS module) must be separately ordered and installed on the mounting rail to the left of the CPU — the CPU does not accept 24VDC directly via screw terminals; the PS module infeed and the CPU backplane current budget must both be calculated; max backplane current budget is defined by the PS module rating (e.g. PS 60W = 2.5A @ 24VDC into bus)"
    - "OPC UA server is only available from firmware V2.6 and TIA Portal V15 — CPU 1516-3 PN/DP with firmware V1.x or V2.0/V2.1 does NOT support OPC UA; always check the CPU firmware version before designing an OPC UA architecture; firmware update requires a new or reformatted SIMATIC Memory Card"
    - "Motion control technology objects (MC) require the technology license — from TIA Portal V14 motion control FBs are licensed per axis; the CPU 1516-3 supports up to 4 motion axes total; for more axes or kinematic transformations use the CPU 1516T-3 PN/DP (Technology CPU variant) which supports CNC kinematics and cam disk editors"
    - "The PROFIBUS interface X3 and PROFINET interface X1 operate independently with separate IP/DP address spaces — they do NOT bridge or route between each other automatically; to route between PROFINET and PROFIBUS devices use the CPU routing functionality (enable in TIA Portal network view) or a dedicated CP 1616 / IE/PB link gateway module"
    - "The S7-1500 mounting rail is NOT compatible with S7-300 or S7-400 mounting systems — S7-300 signal modules, power supplies and the IM 153 interface modules are physically and electrically incompatible with S7-1500 rails; migration from S7-300/400 to S7-1500 requires new hardware including rail, PS, CPU and I/O modules; STEP 7 project migration via TIA Portal migration tool is recommended but requires manual program review"
compatibility:
  sw: "TIA Portal STEP 7 V12+ (V12-V19+); STEP 7 Classic V5.x NOT compatible; TIA Portal Professional for SCL + Graph + Safety; PLCSIM Advanced for simulation"
  languages: "Ladder Diagram (LAD);Function Block Diagram (FBD);Statement List (STL/IL);Structured Control Language (SCL/ST);S7-GRAPH (SFC);Cause and Effect Matrix"
  frameworks: "IEC61131-3;TIA Portal;PROFINET-IRT-RT;PROFIBUS-DPV0-V1-V2;Modbus-TCP-RTU-via-CM;S7-comm;OPC-UA;Web-Server;PROFIsafe-via-F-modules;PROFIdrive;PLCopen-MC"
  certifications: "CE;cULus;UL;FM;RCM;EAC;UKCA;Marine-DNV-GL;IEC61511-SIL2-via-F-variant"

